  "notes": "University Park. The entire HCDD department catalog was missing -- added minimal entries in new hcdd_catalog.json. Every HCDD-sequence course (264/311/340/361/364W/411/412/440) accepts 'HCDD 311' as an equivalent alternate to 'IST 311' (which doesn't exist in the catalog) -- consistently picking the HCDD-prefixed course throughout keeps the whole chain self-satisfying with no gaps, unlike several other majors built this session. Semester 1's fetched credit total (16) didn't match the sum of its originally-listed items (13) -- added an extra 3cr GEN ED item to close the gap, likely dropped by the extraction. 'IST 495' (Internship, listed as a 1cr Summer course) is scheduled as a regular-term item since the engine paces by credit cap, not literal summer/fall/spring labels. The 12-credit 'Application Focus Selection' pool (Data Sciences, Digital Arts and Communication, GIS, Healthcare, Informatics, Psychology, Security and Risk, Sociology, or custom) is modeled generically, same convention as CMPSC's own open pools. Real prereq-fix fallout: STAT 200 now requires MATH 21, which itself requires MATH 4 and MATH 3 -- a full remedial placement chain never otherwise scheduled in this plan, and nothing else in this plan literally needs the STAT 200 course code -- added STAT 100 (Statistical Concepts and Reasoning, no prereq, same STAT department) as a fallback option instead of chasing the remedial chain; the item now resolves to STAT 100 (3cr instead of 4cr). HANDBOOK VERIFICATION PASS: the STAT 100 workaround above was based on a stale assumption -- MATH 21 does NOT actually require MATH 4/MATH 3 (verified against the current catalog: MATH 21's prereq_groups is empty; its real prereq, 'MATH 4 or satisfactory performance on the mathematics placement examination,' is a placement gate, not a literal course requirement, same fact already established for DATSC/ETI/AIMA/IEC/SRA). Restored the real bulletin-required 'STAT 200' (dropping the invented STAT 100 substitute, which the bulletin never actually lists as an alternative for this major) and added a standalone Semester 1 'MATH 21' item (no MATH 3/MATH 4 needed) so it's genuinely completed a term ahead of STAT 200. Bumped max_credits_per_semester 16 -> 19 to fit the extra 3 credits into Semester 1 without displacing anything else, matching the cap already used by IEC. Also: the live bulletin's 'Application Focus Area Course Codes' section (further down the same page cited as this plan's source) enumerates the exact course-by-course list for all 8 focus areas (Data Sciences, Digital Arts and Communication, Geographic Information Systems, Health Care, Informatics, Psychology, Security and Risk, Sociology) -- wired all 4 'Application Focus Selection' items with a 'match' regex built from that real list (the '(400-level)' item restricted to only the 400+-numbered entries), same convention as CMPSC's curated technical-elective lists and CYBER/DATSC's own Application Focus fixes this pass. These remain unfilled recommendation placeholders (not actively recommended, like CMPSC's own curated slots), and the 'must all come from one track' coherence rule isn't enforced -- deferred simplifications, not bugs.",
